(6367519, 943667, 35545, '<td valign="top">There are a lot of interesting textures here, but they get lost in the overall gray tone of the shot.  Needs some blacks.</td>', 'There are a lot of interesting textures here, but they get lost in the overall gray tone of the shot.  Needs some blacks.', '2011-03-30 11:50:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367523, 943627, 35545, '<td valign="top">Beautiful detail and range of tones.</td>', 'Beautiful detail and range of tones.', '2011-03-30 11:52:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367530, 943453, 16148, '<td valign="top">You were in a hurry to shoot the peppers...  Maybe you were hungry?  Anyway, you got the shot before the expiration date.  Actually, I like the plastic wrap with the peppers and your modern spin on the challenge.  I wonder what Edward would think?</td>', 'You were in a hurry to shoot the peppers...  Maybe you were hungry?  Anyway, you got the shot before the expiration date.  Actually, I like the plastic wrap with the peppers and your modern spin on the challenge.  I wonder what Edward would think?', '2011-03-30 11:53:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367534, 943282, 16148, '<td valign="top">Very well done.</td>', 'Very well done.', '2011-03-30 11:55:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367551, 943603, 16148, '<td valign="top">Nice capture but why not black and white?</td>', 'Nice capture but why not black and white?', '2011-03-30 12:02:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367562, 942997, 16148, '<td valign="top">I like your lines and composition.  Seems a little to sharp in areas for Weston but it''s a nice image.</td>', 'I like your lines and composition.  Seems a little to sharp in areas for Weston but it''s a nice image.', '2011-03-30 12:09:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367568, 943488, 10785, '<td valign="top">I think you got a good environmental portrait style going on here, which some of Weston''s portraits were prone to being. I like the black and white toning however I think you could have dialed back shadows a little. Perhaps it is too much contrast. Also, it looks like you weren''t using the blur to create artistic merit which is good because Weston''s work was typically in focus and sharp as far as I could tell. However having the subject be in focus is essential for Weston''s environmental portrait style.</td>', 'I think you got a good environmental portrait style going on here, which some of Weston''s portraits were prone to being. I like the black and white toning however I think you could have dialed back shadows a little. Perhaps it is too much contrast. Also, it looks like you weren''t using the blur to create artistic merit which is good because Weston''s work was typically in focus and sharp as far as I could tell. However having the subject be in focus is essential for Weston''s environmental portrait style.', '2011-03-30 12:11:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367579, 942701, 10785, '<td valign="top">Such a great job on this!! I love how you got the dark blacks and maintained the detail in the whites. Very good "in the style of" photo without being a copy!</td>', 'Such a great job on this!! I love how you got the dark blacks and maintained the detail in the whites. Very good "in the style of" photo without being a copy!', '2011-03-30 12:17:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367586, 943037, 10785, '<td valign="top">This is good. Weston''s cabbage shot was all about the form and the texture. Here, you got the form well but with a different perspective. Lettuce has a different texture which is shown nicely here being smooth and veiny with a sheen. One thing that sticks out is with the background being soooo deep black, the subject looks very two-dimensional. You got the light draping on the subject fairly well!</td>', 'This is good. Weston''s cabbage shot was all about the form and the texture. Here, you got the form well but with a different perspective. Lettuce has a different texture which is shown nicely here being smooth and veiny with a sheen. One thing that sticks out is with the background being soooo deep black, the subject looks very two-dimensional. You got the light draping on the subject fairly well!', '2011-03-30 12:20:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367593, 942410, 10785, '<td valign="top">Nice form study. I like the composition here with the angle. I think there is just not enough light and it is a bit underexposed leaving it kind of grey. Rather than using a longer shutter speed, I think leaving that the same and getting some more light on the subject would have helped. I am no pro though... all my images came out real flat!!</td>', 'Nice form study. I like the composition here with the angle. I think there is just not enough light and it is a bit underexposed leaving it kind of grey. Rather than using a longer shutter speed, I think leaving that the same and getting some more light on the subject would have helped. I am no pro though... all my images came out real flat!!', '2011-03-30 12:24:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367598, 943652, 10785, '<td valign="top">Very good stylistic photo without being a copy of a subject. (As far as I have seen I have never seen him shoot a fan of any kind anyway). Excellent lighting and exposure. Really good shadow keeping detail in the blacks while allowing for detailed highlights with out being overblown.</td>', 'Very good stylistic photo without being a copy of a subject. (As far as I have seen I have never seen him shoot a fan of any kind anyway). Excellent lighting and exposure. Really good shadow keeping detail in the blacks while allowing for detailed highlights with out being overblown.', '2011-03-30 12:26:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367600, 943365, 47470, '<td valign="top">This is one of the most attempted shots in this challenge, but no one came as close to nailing it as you did.  Wonderful use of light.</td>', 'This is one of the most attempted shots in this challenge, but no one came as close to nailing it as you did.  Wonderful use of light.', '2011-03-30 12:27:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367602, 943282, 47470, '<td valign="top">The light and the texture in this are very Weston.  The addition of the textured background made this.</td>', 'The light and the texture in this are very Weston.  The addition of the textured background made this.', '2011-03-30 12:28:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367604, 943627, 47470, '<td valign="top">Now that''s Weston texture.</td>', 'Now that''s Weston texture.', '2011-03-30 12:28:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367605, 943598, 16148, '<td valign="top">NIce find and well seen.  I know John will appreciate this tribute.  Gave me a good laugh too.  Looks like a pretty good likeness based on his self portraits.</td>', 'NIce find and well seen.  I know John will appreciate this tribute.  Gave me a good laugh too.  Looks like a pretty good likeness based on his self portraits.', '2011-03-30 12:29:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367608, 942876, 47470, '<td valign="top">This is gorgeous.  The control of the light is perfect, highlighting the bright flowers just enough to prevent the image from being swallowed by all the black.</td>', 'This is gorgeous.  The control of the light is perfect, highlighting the bright flowers just enough to prevent the image from being swallowed by all the black.', '2011-03-30 12:31:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367612, 942748, 47470, '<td valign="top">The texture on this is great, though I would have liked to see a few more tones in the brighter end of the scale too.</td>', 'The texture on this is great, though I would have liked to see a few more tones in the brighter end of the scale too.', '2011-03-30 12:32:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367619, 943008, 47470, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful, but from what I know about Weston, he used small apertures and long exposures to achieve deep depths of field.  Not knocking you for that, though, since this is so pretty.</td>', 'This is beautiful, but from what I know about Weston, he used small apertures and long exposures to achieve deep depths of field.  Not knocking you for that, though, since this is so pretty.', '2011-03-30 12:36:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(6367621, 943453, 47470, '<td valign="top">Lovely BnW conversion.  I was a bit iffy on the slight angle of the subject, but the more I look at it, the more I think symmetry would have made it too stiff.  This definitely captures how Weston made the every-day into art.</td>', 'Lovely BnW conversion.  I was a bit iffy on the slight angle of the subject, but the more I look at it, the more I think symmetry would have made it too stiff.  This definitely captures how Weston made the every-day into art.', '2011-03-30 12:39:09.000000', NULL, 1),
