(6376416, 943603, 23141, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EL-ROI:</b></div><hr/><i> If Weston shot in color, he may have photographed this... maybe. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/><a href="//ccp.uair.arizona.edu/item/15395" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//ccp.uair.arizona.edu/item/15395</a> <br/> <br/>I''ve gotta admit, this comment burned my ass all through voting, because I''d done my research and you hadn''t.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2011-04-06 11:04:53.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by EL-ROI: If Weston shot in color, he may have photographed this... maybe.   //ccp.uair.arizona.edu/item/15395  I''ve gotta admit, this comment burned my ass all through voting, because I''d done my research and you hadn''t.', '2011-04-06 12:04:01.000000', '2011-04-06 12:04:53.000000', 0),
(6376561, 942876, 54033, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by EL-ROI:</b></div><hr/><i> Look at that, you used f11... wonder how you got such a short focal length at 60mm.<br/> <br/>Guessing the subject distance and inputing your stats in DOF calculator you get the following results:<br/> <br/><b>Subject distance 	3 ft<br/> <br/>Depth of field <br/>Near limit 	2.85 ft<br/>Far limit 	3.16 ft<br/>Total 	0.31 ft<br/> <br/>In front of subject 	0.15 ft	(47%)<br/>Behind subject 	0.16 ft	(53%)</b> <br/> <br/>............................................<br/> <br/><b>Subject distance 	5 ft<br/> <br/>Depth of field <br/>Near limit 	4.6 ft<br/>Far limit 	5.48 ft<br/>Total 	0.88 ft<br/> <br/>In front of subject 	0.4 ft	(46%)<br/>Behind subject 	0.48 ft	(54%)</b> <br/> <br/>.............................................<br/> <br/><b>Subject distance 	6 ft<br/> <br/>Depth of field <br/>Near limit 	5.43 ft<br/>Far limit 	6.71 ft<br/>Total 	1.28 ft<br/> <br/>In front of subject 	0.57 ft	(45%)<br/>Behind subject 	0.71 ft	(55%)</b> <br/> <br/>.............................................<br/> <br/><b>Subject distance 	8 ft<br/> <br/>Depth of field <br/>Near limit 	7.01 ft<br/>Far limit 	9.32 ft<br/>Total 	2.32 ft<br/> <br/>In front of subject 	0.99 ft	(43%)<br/>Behind subject 	1.32 ft	(57%)</b> <br/> <br/>sorry for cluttering up your comments... just going to school on your image!! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>(The distance was &lt; 12 cm) It''s a miniature cactus <br/> <br/>Thanks <br/> <br/>Tareq</td>', 'Originally posted by EL-ROI: Look at that, you used f11... wonder how you got such a short focal length at 60mm. Guessing the subject distance and inputing your stats in DOF calculator you get the following results: Subject distance 	3 ft Depth of field Near limit 	2.85 ftFar limit 	3.16 ftTotal 	0.31 ft In front of subject 	0.15 ft	(47%)Behind subject 	0.16 ft	(53%)  ............................................ Subject distance 	5 ft Depth of field Near limit 	4.6 ftFar limit 	5.48 ftTotal 	0.88 ft In front of subject 	0.4 ft	(46%)Behind subject 	0.48 ft	(54%)  ............................................. Subject distance 	6 ft Depth of field Near limit 	5.43 ftFar limit 	6.71 ftTotal 	1.28 ft In front of subject 	0.57 ft	(45%)Behind subject 	0.71 ft	(55%)  ............................................. Subject distance 	8 ft Depth of field Near limit 	7.01 ftFar limit 	9.32 ftTotal 	2.32 ft In front of subject 	0.99 ft	(43%)Behind subject 	1.32 ft	(57%)  sorry for cluttering up your comments... just going to school on your image!!   (The distance was < 12 cm) It''s a miniature cactus  Thanks  Tareq', '2011-04-06 13:10:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6376594, 943290, 16106, '<td valign="top">One of the most Westonian (if that''s a word) images in the challenge. Sadly many of those who truly nailed the challenge ended up here in the middle of the pack. What most stood out for me in this image was the way you got the skin tone just the way he did, so it looks like marble, well done.</td>', 'One of the most Westonian (if that''s a word) images in the challenge. Sadly many of those who truly nailed the challenge ended up here in the middle of the pack. What most stood out for me in this image was the way you got the skin tone just the way he did, so it looks like marble, well done.', '2011-04-06 13:25:52.000000', NULL, 0),
